In fall 2017, Jeter became part-owner and chief executive officer of the National League's Miami Marlins.
In January 2020, the ex-Yankees shortstop was voted into the Baseball Hall of Fame. He appeared on 396 of the 397 ballots cast by members of the Baseball Writers' Association of America to fall just shy of joining former teammate Mariano Rivera as the only players to earn unanimous selection.
Personal
Off the field, Derek Jeter garnered attention for his quiet confidence and good looks. He was romantically linked to several high-profile women, including pop singer Mariah Carey and actress Minka Kelly. Along with appearing in numerous commercials, he signed a deal with Avon Products, Inc., in 2006 to create a fragrance for men called Driven.
Jeter also used his celebrity and his prominent position as a sports star to help children. In 1996, he established the Turn 2 Foundation to encourage young people to be healthy and academically successful, to become leaders, and to stay away from drugs and alcohol. The foundation supports and creates programs to achieve these goals.
In October 2015, Jeter proposed to his girlfriend Hannah Davis. The couple tied the knot in July 2016. Their first child, daughter Bella Raine Jeter, was born on August 17, 2017.
